**﴿For they﴾**: that is, as a consequence of your seeing them and your description of them as you have mentioned, I am informing you with an emphatic statement that they are

Since the form *fa'ūl* is used for intensification (*al-mubālaga*), it suffices for both the enemy and the friend, so there is no need for the plural form, especially as it resembles verbal nouns (*maṣādir*) such as *qabūl* and *ṣahīl*. Therefore, reporting about the plural pronoun, He said: **﴿an enemy to me﴾**, that is, I treat them as an opponent with evil and deal with them in their destruction and annihilation as one deals with enemies, and with everyone who worships them, as He said in the other verse: **﴿You and your forefathers were certainly in manifest error﴾** (al-Anbiya: 54), **﴿Fie upon you and what you worship besides God﴾** (al-Anbiya: 67), and **﴿By God, I will surely plot against your idols﴾** (al-Anbiya: 57).

Since they were polytheists, and among their forefathers of old there were those who worshipped God alone, He said: **﴿except the Lord of the worlds﴾**, that is, the Manager of all these existences, as Moses (peace be upon him) said, because that is the most well-known and most evident of attributes, for He is not an enemy to me, but rather He is my Protector and my Worshipped One;
